In news:<1119451721.781467.261070@g14g2000cwa.googlegroups.com>, Cyde 
Weys <cyde@umd.edu> says...
> So I'm sitting around pudding farming when one drops an unidentified
> wand.  I try engrave-testing it and it is a wand of polymorph.  YES!!!
> However, I have no idea what to do with it, as there are so many
> possibilities ...
> Should I,
> A) Polymorph myself?  I have a ring of polymorph control but no dragon
> armor, so I'm thinking I could polymorph myself into a gray dragon, lay
> some eggs, kill them for the scales, and then make a gray dragon scale
> mail?

Ehhh.. That sounds like a hideously bad idea. Rasing baby dragons is a 
slow process and I think that petkillers (filicide even!) are 
disapproved of even by the chaotic gods.
Roleplaying-wise it would put you way off the chaotic end of the scale 
IMHO.

> B) Polymorph my pet?  I don't have a good pet and this could be really
> useful.  Only problem is it's kind of risky and I might totally use up
> the wand of polymorph without getting anything good.

This is what polytraps are for. And they are usually available for free 
and can be used an infinite number of times.

> C) Polymorph items?  I'm in a pudding farm right now so naturally there
> are a lot of items laying about.  Should I try polypiling and hope for
> a magic marker or other useful goods?

Could be fun to try. The chance to get a magical tool out of non-magical 
ones is virtually negligible. Consult the polypiling section of the 
wands spoiler.

D) Save it and zap some threatening bad guy with it and hopefully watch 
him turn into something meek.

I'd go for C, then D, then B and perhaps A (but *not* for the 'female 
dragon -> eggs -> baby dragons -> filicide -> scales -> scale mail' 
idea).

